caption: Scope and Precedence

These numerical standards govern applicable Mastery requirements across Origins and Engines, including Skilled and Hybrid Traditions. Except for the explicit Engine exceptions below, every Tier 2 Tradition requires at least 100 character points invested in qualifying Tradition advancement and every Tier 3 Tradition requires at least 300 character points invested in qualifying Tradition advancement. Regular, Ritual, Inspired, Realm, and Word Traditions are exempt from that ordinary character-point investment floor and instead use their Engine-specific Mastery structures. Realm Mastery requires purchasing the Tradition's required Realms to maximum, but no additional 100/300-point floor beyond those Realm purchases. Word Mastery uses its lexicon, skill, and any actual Word-purchase requirements without an additional 100/300-point floor. Enhancement Traditions replace the ordinary Tier 3 investment floor with the cumulative generation-and-sharing requirement below. The other listed governing-trait and characteristic thresholds still apply where relevant. These standards replace conflicting numerical Mastery benchmarks in Engine defaults and individual Traditions; a local statement allowing a stricter or different numerical benchmark does not override them.
